<Base
  title="Privacy Policy â€” AdaptiveResume"
  description="What AdaptiveResume collects and why, how your career documents are protected, how identifiers are separated before AI analysis, how long we keep things, and how to delete your data."
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Your resume is some of the most personal data there is â€” your whole working life on a page.
        This policy explains what we collect, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and what you
        can do about it.
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          AdaptiveResume LLC is a Georgia limited liability company. You can reach us at
          <a href="mailto:support@adaptiveresume.com">support@adaptiveresume.com</a> or by mail at
          AdaptiveResume LLC, 8735 Dunwoody Place, Suite N, Atlanta, Georgia 30350. This policy
          explains what we collect, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and what you can do about
          it. It applies to adaptiveresume.com and app.adaptiveresume.com.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account data:</strong> email address, hashed password (or auth provider ID), purchase history.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Career documents you provide:</strong> up to three resumes and, optionally, your
            LinkedIn resume export. These are sensitive by nature â€” they describe your work history
            and can incidentally reveal more (see Â§9). <strong>Please do not include information
            about your health, a disability, a medical condition, or a diagnosis in the files you
            upload. We do not need it, we do not ask for it, and we do not analyze it.</strong>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Content you create in the Service:</strong> confirmations, edits, skips, notes,
            your finished resume.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Payment data:</strong> processed by Stripe; we never receive or store your card
            number. We receive transaction status and last-4/brand for receipts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical data: our application uses your IP address only as an in-memory key for
            rate-limiting and abuse prevention; we do not store it in our database, and it is
            discarded whenever the service restarts or is redeployed. We do not store your IP address
            ourselves, though our infrastructure providers may log it briefly at the platform level
            for security and operations, such as hosting and authentication logs, and Google receives
            it transiently for coarse geolocation as part of analytics. Our application code never
            reads or stores your browser type or user agent. On our marketing pages, Google Analytics
            and Google Ads conversion measurement separately collect your browser type, operating
            system, device category, and the date and time of your visit; we use these tools for
            analytics and conversion measurement, with Google Signals disabled, an opt-out toggle,
            and Global Privacy Control honored before any tag loads, but we do not use them for
            advertising personalization or cross-site tracking.</strong>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Free scan:</strong> runs without an account; scan files are processed in memory
            and not stored or logged.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Launch list and feedback: your email address if you join the pre-launch list, and
            anything you choose to tell us about a past resume-service experience. Every question is
            optional, including your email address. Feedback stays internal; if we ever share what we
            learn, it is in aggregate, never with names, yours or anyone else's. If you ask us to
            delete your data, that request covers your launch-list entry and any feedback you
            submitted that carries your email address.</strong>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          To provide the Service you asked for (extract, redact, analyze, propose, assemble, deliver);
          to process payments; to send transactional email (confirmations, receipts, security
          notices); to protect the Service (rate-limiting, abuse prevention); to meet legal
          obligations. We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for
          cross-context behavioral advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>4. AI processing and PII minimization</h2>
        <p>
          AI-assisted analysis is performed on redacted text. Your name and contact details are
          separated out before any content is sent to our AI provider, and they are re-attached only
          at final assembly on our own systems. Our AI provider is Anthropic, which processes the
          content as a service provider under its commercial API terms. Under those terms, Anthropic
          does not train its models on the inputs or outputs of our API use. Limited exceptions apply
          under Anthropic's own terms, including content that its automated systems flag for safety or
          policy review, which it may retain and review. We do not use consumer AI accounts to process
          your content.
        </p>

        <h2>5. De-identified learning</h2>
        <p>
          The Service records aggregate, occupation-level observations, for example which skills a
          given occupation commonly involves. These observations describe occupations, not people.
          They contain no names, contact details, or other identifiers, and they cannot reasonably be
          used to infer anything about you or to be linked back to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to keep this information in that
          form, including removing identifiers before an observation is recorded and storing the
          observations separately from account data. We publicly commit to maintain and use this
          information only in de-identified form and never to attempt to re-identify it, except to the
          limited extent needed to test whether our own de-identification process is working. We
          contractually require anyone who receives this information to do the same. We keep these
          observations indefinitely, because they describe occupations rather than individuals.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Subprocessors</h2>
        <table class="subprocessors">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Vendor</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Region</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Stripe</td>
              <td>Payments</td>
              <td>US</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Supabase</td>
              <td>Database, authentication, storage</td>
              <td>United States (Ohio)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Anthropic</td>
              <td>AI-assisted analysis (redacted content only)</td>
              <td>US</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Render</td>
              <td>Application and site hosting</td>
              <td>United States (Virginia)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Brevo</td>
              <td>Transactional email</td>
              <td>European Union</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>ImprovMX</td>
              <td>Inbound email forwarding for support@</td>
              <td>United States (mail servers located in France)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          We will update this table before adding a subprocessor that handles personal data. We do not
          sell your personal information to any of them, and each is engaged to process personal
          information only for the purposes described in this policy. Support email sent to
          <a href="mailto:support@adaptiveresume.com">support@adaptiveresume.com</a> is routed through
          ImprovMX, our inbound mail-forwarding vendor. ImprovMX stores each message until it is
          successfully forwarded to us, after which the message is deleted; if delivery fails, the
          message may be held for up to seven days, and delivery metadata such as the subject line,
          sender, and recipient is retained for up to seven days, though message bodies are not logged
          beyond the forwarding process. Because Brevo's servers are located in the European Union and
          ImprovMX's mail servers are located in France, sending information to those vendors involves
          an international transfer of personal information. Our agreement with Brevo already
          incorporates the Standard Contractual Clauses. We are working to put equivalent contractual
          protections in place with ImprovMX.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Retention</h2>
        <p>
          In-progress review drafts are deleted automatically after seven days of inactivity, enforced
          by a scheduled sweep.
        </p>
        <p>
          The files you upload are not stored. They are processed and discarded, and the working text
          extracted from them lives inside your draft and is deleted with the draft, at most seven
          days after your last activity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Files submitted through the free scan are processed in memory and are never stored.
        </p>
        <p>
          Finished resumes in My Files are kept until you delete them. You can delete any individual
          file at any time, and deleting your account removes all of them. Deleting your account does
          not delete your account and purchase records, which we retain separately as described below.
        </p>
        <p>
          Account and purchase records are kept for at least seven years to meet tax and accounting
          obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our transactional email log â€” the recipient address, subject line, delivery status, and
          timestamp, never the message body â€” is kept until you ask us to delete it or you
          unsubscribe.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your launch-list entry and any feedback you submit, described in Section 2, are kept until
          you ask us to delete them or you unsubscribe.
        </p>
        <p>
          Aggregate occupation-level observations, described in Section 5, are kept indefinitely.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We protect your information with encryption in transit and at rest. Drafts and stored
          deliverables are additionally sealed with application-layer AES-256-GCM encryption.
          Confirmation tokens are hashed and expire after 14 days. Access to systems is granted on a
          least-privilege basis. No method of storage or transmission is perfect. If a breach affects
          your personal information, we will notify you without undue delay and as required by
          applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Sensitive inferences in career documents</h2>
        <p>
          Resumes can incidentally reveal things such as union membership, citizenship or immigration
          status, military or veteran status, religious affiliation, or a disability accommodation. We
          do not seek out that information, we do not ask for it, and we do not analyze it or use it to
          infer anything about you. The Service proposes work-relevant skills and credentials for you
          to confirm, and nothing more. Where information of this kind appears in a file you provide,
          we collect and process it only to produce the document you asked for, never for the purpose
          of inferring characteristics about you, and we protect it the same way we protect the rest
          of your information.
        </p>
        <p>
          We ask again that you not include health, medical, or disability information in the files
          you upload. If you already have, email
          <a href="mailto:support@adaptiveresume.com">support@adaptiveresume.com</a>; because we do
          not keep a separate copy of the file you uploaded, as described in Section 7, we will delete
          the draft or finished resume that contains it rather than a separately stored file.
        </p>

        <h2 id="your-privacy-choices">10. Your rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Everyone:</strong> access, correct, download, or delete your data by emailing
            <a href="mailto:support@adaptiveresume.com">support@adaptiveresume.com</a> or using
            in-account tools; delete your account at any time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>California: where the California Consumer Privacy Act applies to us, California
            residents have the rights to know, delete, correct, and receive a portable copy of their
            personal information, and the right not to be treated differently for exercising them. We
            do not sell personal information and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral
            advertising, so no opt-out link is required. Any sensitive information that reaches us
            does so incidentally and is not used to infer characteristics about you, so no separate
            right-to-limit link is required. We honor authorized-agent requests with verification. As
            a practical matter we extend these rights to everyone who asks, wherever they live.</strong>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Outside the United States: the Service is offered from and directed to the United
            States, and we do not target it to residents of the European Union or the United Kingdom.
            If that changes, we will update this policy before it does.</strong>
          </li>
          <li>
            We respond to verified requests within 45 days, and we will tell you if we need more time.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>11. Children</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is not directed to anyone under 18, we do not knowingly collect personal
          information from anyone under 18, and our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> require
          account holders to be at least 18. If we learn that we have collected information from
          someone under 18, we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Prospective updates with a new "Last updated" date; material changes announced to account
          holders by email at least 14 days ahead.
        </p>

        <p class="effective">Last updated: 09/01/2026</p>
